# geom_binner_arena_bounds — the GEOM.BINNER arena bound, proved on the module
# zhao_geom_binner actually instantiates (ZH-058 / ZH-026; design/blocks.yml
# names this file as the block's formal lane). Run with cwd = tests/formal.
#
# TWO TASKS, both required:
#   prove — P1..P5: the occupancy never passes CHUNKS, a GRANT always names a
#           chunk strictly inside the arena ("never scribble", the ledger's own
#           words), a full arena refuses every request, the pointer strictly
#           increases by exactly one per grant between releases (so two grants
#           never name the same chunk), and a release empties the arena in one
#           cycle. Every one of those is ONE-STEP INDUCTIVE, so `mode prove`
#           (temporal induction) closes them for ALL time — which is the whole
#           reason this is not a bmc task: the interesting state, a FULL arena,
#           is 256 grants from reset and no bounded run of a sane depth reaches
#           it.
#   cover — the interesting states are REACHABLE, shown on a deliberately tiny
#           second instance (CHUNKS = 4) in the same harness: a grant happens,
#           the arena fills, a full arena refuses a request, and a release
#           re-arms a full arena. Without this task P1 and P3 would also hold
#           for an allocator that never granted anything, and the proof would
#           say nothing.
#
# SCOPE — stated plainly. This proves the ARENA BOUND, which is the safety half
# of "safe overflow" and the half that can corrupt memory. It does NOT prove
# the binner's overflow POLICY (which triangle is dropped, when the frame wall
# goes up, that at most one triangle per frame is partially binned) — that is
# behaviour over a large FSM with four RAMs, out of reach for this engine, and
# it is covered instead by the directed lane's tri-store and arena overflow
# cases and by the differential lanes against zref::Binner.
#
# Nor does it prove the corner test, the enumeration order or the tile
# indexing: those are 36-bit affine arithmetic over a 576-entry tile RAM, and
# they are covered by geom_binner_directed / _random (soundness against
# zref::EdgeWalk over every tile of the grid).
#
# Frontend: read_slang (the lane choice since W2.3). No package dependencies:
# zhao_geom_arena.sv is self-contained, so nothing is staged or copied.

[tasks]
prove
cover

[options]
prove: mode prove
prove: depth 4
cover: mode cover
cover: depth 12
expect pass

[engines]
smtbmc boolector

[script]
read_slang --top geom_binner_arena_bounds_fv zhao_geom_arena.sv geom_binner_arena_bounds_fv.sv
prep -top geom_binner_arena_bounds_fv

[files]
../../fpga/rtl/geometry/zhao_geom_arena.sv
geom_binner_arena_bounds_fv.sv
